message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Car.Ma._Cell: paired analysis of mitochondrial networks in fluorescence micrographs"
version: 1.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/colivieri89/Car.Ma._Cell"
authors:
  - family-names: Olivieri
    given-names: Carlo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3548-846X"
    affiliation: "Department of Engineering, Pegaso Telematic University, Naples, Italy"
  - family-names: Negri
    given-names: Mariarosaria
  - family-names: Sessa
    given-names: Salvatore
abstract: >-
  Desktop application and Python library for the quantitative comparison of
  the mitochondrial networks of two cells imaged by fluorescence microscopy.
  Both images are brought to a common physical resolution from their scale
  bars and processed with the same parameters: background subtraction,
  optional Richardson-Lucy deconvolution, tubeness enhancement, automatic
  thresholding, skeletonisation and extraction of the skeleton graph. The
  program reports topology, branch lengths, density, branching,
  connectivity, fragmentation, network complexity, object shape, fractal
  dimension and node-degree distribution of each cell, side by side, with
  figures, CSV and JSON files and an Excel workbook.
keywords:
  - mitochondria
  - mitochondrial network
  - fluorescence microscopy
  - image analysis
  - skeletonisation
  - graph analysis
  - fusion
  - fission
